{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa74-c329-7d72-8811-c1901bb53d47"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260909-2ez769, status=development)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Preserve and verify all foreign RPC bytes and checkpointed SSH/peer work; isolate only enumerated RPC delta and use managed current-base transition before credentials implementation.\n- [ ] Implement exact closed Config4 and Host Trust Store readers; refuse missing, partial, unreadable, ambiguous or downgraded state without implicit legacy fallback.\n- [ ] Implement explicit out-of-band enrollment, unique credential-to-host mapping, fresh-key bounded rotation, immediate revocation and current-generation mutation authorization through production APIs.\n- [ ] Provide owner-only credential custody and atomic crash-durable trust writes, with platform custody and crash/recovery evidence and no secret replication.\n- [ ] Implement exact-preview confirmed Config4 migration, complete peer enrollment, durable apply and rollback while preserving accepted Config1/2/3 and SSH/peer behavior.\n- [ ] Demonstrate complete pinned v0.6.0 sections 6.6 and 11.10.2/3 acceptance through positive and narrowing-negative production tests; preserve truthful mutation controls and exact-source results; pass required local checks.\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260909-2ez769\n- **Title:** TASK-260909-2ez769: implement-host-credentials-and-config4-migration\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-1kiyj6\n\n### Description\n\nImplement machine-local Host Trust Store 1.0.0, issuance and explicit enrollment, rotation/revocation and authorization generations, and explicit Configuration 4.0.0 migration. Preserve accepted historical Config 1/2/3 and peer identity/SSH work; consume it through reviewed integration. This is pending runtime work, not delivered by catalogue adoption.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6; sections 6.6, 11.10.2, 11.10.3. Own credential custody and trust-generation APIs, durable preview/apply/rollback and credential exclusion; RPC transport/admission stays TASK-260830-z1yxg9, conformance TASK-260830-2x16gz.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nExact closed Config-4 and Host Trust Store readers; explicit out-of-band enrollment, unique credential-to-host mapping, fresh-key bounded rotation and immediate revocation; current-generation mutation authorization; owner-only atomic crash-durable writes; exact-preview confirmed Config-4 migration with complete peer enrollment; refuse partial/unreadable/missing state, downgrade and implicit legacy fallback. Positive and narrowing-negative production tests, platform custody and crash evidence; no secret replication. Resume only after signed STORY-260908-18woqo lands.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4190`\n- Content digest: `sha256:d3bef7ae84af0f92b4c4a7ac2563d018075992f43e5d1e7e13238dbc3f26e9ab`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2958`\n- Content digest: `sha256:74609054ec9524be4f3f932e107edf394a100181c674252115117b17851c0cce`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_resume-after-pr207.md\nResume preserved credentials/config implementation after root confirms PR207 is landed and the canonical Curator CLI is installed. This is a recovery of completed work, not a fresh implementation. Read results.md, retry2.md, retry3.md and the retained validation failures. Prior run de0df2 was deliberately cancelled to stop deterministic repeated gate21 failures, not because its candidate was discarded.\nVerify actual canonical CLI provenance and refresh-candidate help before using it. Preserve the RPC backup manifest (15 files) and parked delta; do not absorb RPC into this leaf. Preserve checkpointed SSH/peer work and all hosttrust/Config4 changes. The shared Story base must move from c1eff01 to current protected AX trunk containing the v0.6.0 adoption. Combine current trunk coherently with the candidate, resolve real conflicts preserving both intended changes, and use the repaired explicit managed refresh-candidate from the live producer with its exclusive lease. Do not selectively vendor catalogue files merely to make gate21 pass, weaken validation, edit board registries, or manually synthesize checkpoint commits.\nRefresh preserves candidate bytes rather than merging incoming source for you; verify the resulting complete candidate incorporates the adopted catalogue/specpin/ownership/config contracts. If replay conflicts require a supported resolution packet, bind exact checkpoint/path/content digests. Any further reusable tool defect goes to root with evidence; no unchanged doomed handoff or retry storm.\nRun applicable local validation on the refreshed candidate, with exact-head/source provenance. Reconcile new source and negative evidence from retry3. Full scope and accepted RPC caller boundary remain; no invented guarantees for dispatch after shared-lock release or Windows DACL validation. Publish the normal next CR through handoff only once prerequisites are satisfied. Do not integrate or push main. Independent review will follow.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-current-base.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-current-base.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2815`\n- Content digest: `sha256:70f5f797cfdf81e5a2b274846e317223c2cbbbdf1c4b41b59fe46d09dc70acd8`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev3.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev3.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3001`\n- Content digest: `sha256:553782db41a386bdf1c444d40fbca3ff396aa0a0913e59e6ea0d46d7f7bc7ada`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2426`\n- Content digest: `sha256:bd0585b3521067e2cbe22909ee6deb2ae86e7b8ff727b0be583fce953f896a6b`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3-current.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-after-rev3-current.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3388`\n- Content digest: `sha256:bac7ff39d3935a3998425dd06b28bf6c765aae293118d2e00e36da053a9e7765`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev4.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev4.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5824`\n- Content digest: `sha256:53167f936d6b2ed658b2802cd25dd132247b26e9bb7db9e6b9d567d7cb0710ff`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_reviewer-cr5.md`\n\n- Byte count: `5242`\n- Content digest: `sha256:475525ab791e46b69f70673f574be35fa008dec5e419593244f4e0fcf0c62b4b`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260909-2ez769_rework-rev5.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260909-