edConfigCopy, a row-21 handoff with notes on seven owning tasks, 19 of 21 rows driven (rows 15 and 21 explicitly not driven), 25+1 hosttrust and 4+1 config plants killed with a neutral SURVIVED control and one documented converge-ignore survivor by the staged-marker backstop. These are producer claims requiring independent verification; in particular decide whether the shared-reader release-then-reacquire path leaves a window in which a second writer stages a new marker between the shared release and the exclusive acquisition, and whether the 500ms lock verification retry can admit a replaced inode. Verify the three CR4 findings against production entry points, RED-first evidence and your own isolated reproduction:\n4|F1 (surviving-process admission): port or rerun TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration and TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader on the exact candidate; the surviving LoadCoherent must refuse or converge, never admit old generation 3/4; confirm the pending joint-commit marker is a general admission barrier across WithSharedSnapshot/readSnapshotLocked, readCommitted, authorization boundaries and mutation transactions, that stale requests are still refused (never silently refreshed), and that TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration now asserts convergence with fatal expectations instead of returning silently on Load/Configuration/Open/ReadSnapshot errors. Cover apply and rollback, surviving and reopened processes, marker cleanup/error ordering. Distinguish tested refusal from proven recovery.\n5|F2 (first-open lock replacement): rerun TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization; with the child paused after the absence observation and the parent holding the lock, the child must end up on the same inode and must not return while the parent holds it; confirm initialization is atomic and non-replacing through production Open, that existing-lock contention is tested, and read the Windows initialization path for the same rule (report Windows execution honestly as unverified where no runtime ran).\n6|F3 (evidence and ownership): native Windows DACL tests must exist as real build-tagged test code driving the production custody entries for owner-only acceptance, other-principal refusal and reparse handling; without a Windows runtime, row 15 is implementation present / runtime unverified, never a pass; config-backup contents must be classified against the applicable custody contract rather than profile-ACL inheritance; row 21 must carry a precise handoff naming each downstream owning task, API and test obligation (check the notes the producer wrote on those tasks) and be counted as not consumer-driven.\n7|\n8|Retain the CR3 repairs (stale generation refusal, same/separate-Store revocation contention) and the corrected config mutation accounting; re-derive the 21-row AC table from source and named tests, counting driven/bounded/failing rows honestly; check that every claimed exit comes from a real command status and that the harmless SURVIVED control was applied through the same harness; no compile-failure, unapplied or empty-selection kills. Confirm the parked RPC artifacts and control-root backup hashes are untouched and that no candidate path overlaps the RPC manifest; confirm checkpointed SSH/peer predecessors are preserved and no RPC transport was implemented.\n9|\n10|Method: isolated immutable probes only (throwaway clone or extracted tree), never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local. Attach TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md and TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev5.zip, complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260909-2ez769, revision=5, evidence=TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev5.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2 classes and repeat-of named. Model: codex gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"