{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c70b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa74-c329-7d72-8811-c1901bb53d47"},"sequence":480,"recorded_at":1780531400000955,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa76-471b-7263-b53f-10c1a635ff0a"},"task_id":"01a0aa76-471b-7263-b53f-10c1a635ff0a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa76-471b-7263-b53f-10c1a635ff0a","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260909-2ez769/TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev5.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-2ez769 rework results rev5 — CR4 findings repaired\n2|\n3|Producer rework after CR4 changes-requested verdict (RUN-260910-faeff7).\n4|Managed base a89328ca85a613abde39660f4be749a8fcf57903 (v0.6.0 adoption trunk\n5|in place; no base move needed). Worktree left UNCOMMITTED on\n6|task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 for handoff snapshot; no producer\n7|commit, no main push. Producer: Muse (muse-spark), 2026-09-16.\n8|\n9|RED-first: the exact reviewer probes were ported onto pre-fix source and\n10|reproduced FAIL (exit 1 each, logs in evidence tarball); the committed\n11|tests below keep the same behavior under producer names so a future\n12|reviewer drop-in cannot collide on test/type names.\n13|\n14|Port mapping (reviewer probe -> committed test):\n15|- TestReviewerCrashBetweenConfigAndGeneration -> TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply\n16|- TestReviewerRollbackCrashSurvivingReader -> TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedRollback\n17|- TestReviewerCrashReopenConverges -> behavior kept by fixed TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration\n18|- TestReviewerCrossProcessLockInitialization -> TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock\n19|- TestReviewerSeparateStoreRevocationDuringBoundary -> TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithSeparateStoreRevocation\n20|- TestReviewerStaleMutation / TestReviewerRevocationDuringBoundary -> kept passing; covered by TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration / TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation\n21|\n22|## Preservation (re-verified this run)\n23|\n24|- 4 tracked RPC paths CLEAN vs HEAD; no UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md or\n25|  internal/rpcwire remnants in the worktree; none of those paths in the\n26|  candidate diff.\n27|- Control-root backup .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910:\n28|  15/15 files match manifest SHA256.\n29|- Parked delta .temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/parked-rpc-delta-260910: 11/11\n30|  untracked files match the control manifest SHA256.\n31|- Checkpointed SSH/peer bytes untouched: candidate touches only config,\n32|  hosttrust, secprim/census_test.go, LOGBOOK.md and the carried\n33|  peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go; zero sshtransport changes.\n34|\n35|## CR4 finding resolutions (production mechanism, not assertions)\n36|\n37|F1 (P1, surviving crash readers) — the pending joint-commit marker is now a\n38|general admission barrier (`internal/hosttrust/joint.go`: `markerPresent`,\n39|`convergeLocked`; `transact.go`: `lockForConvergedRead`):\n40|- Exclusive entry points (transact, JointCommit, WithMutationAuthorization,\n41|  Initialize) converge pending intent before reading; JointCommit converges\n42|  leftovers first (forward completion moves the generation so stale markers\n43|  still refuse; refused leftovers fail the commit with the marker kept).\n44|- Shared readers (ReadSnapshot, WithSharedSnapshot, AuthorizeDispatch) take\n45|  the shared fast path only when no marker is present; otherwise they\n46|  release shared, acquire exclusive (never an in-place upgrade), converge\n47|  or refuse, then read. Marker-absent under a shared hold implies a\n48|  coherent pair, since staging a marker nee