-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n\\n### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework — CR3 changes-requested repaired on base a89328c\\n- SCOPE: same candidate, no base move (adoption trunk already in). All five CR3 findings addressed in `internal/hosttrust` + `internal/config`; no RPC absorption (4 tracked RPC paths verified CLEAN, parked 11/11 intact, no rpcwire remnants).\\n- P1 STALE MUTATION: `WithMutationAuthorization` no longer refreshes the cached generation; a binding older than committed refuses `ErrStaleGeneration` (`authorize.go`). Committed `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration` + narrowing plant `stale-mutation-refresh` (KILLED).\\n- P1 BOUNDARY/REVOKE: lock descriptors are per-acquisition (unix `flock`, Windows `LockFileEx`), so same-process goroutines serialize like separate processes; lock-file creation guarded by a process mutex; `Initialize` no longer re-acquires (unlocked nested read + documented no-reentry discipline). Existing serialization test hardened to the deterministic 250ms contention shape. Narrowing coverage via `revoke-state` + serialization tests.\\n- P1 CRASH ATOMICITY: new joint commit (`joint.go`): closed `PendingCommit` marker, `JointCommit` (in-lock revalidation + marker + replace + bump + unmark), `Recover` (forward/abort/refuse) auto-run by `Open`. `CommitConfigChange` removed (it encoded the split-brain pattern). Apply/rollback revalidate preview/source/generation/custody inside the exclusive hold; post-bump failures restore source + converge via `Recover` (`ErrJointReplacementDurable`). Committed real child-process crash test (`TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, exit 77) plus abort/intervention/already-bumped/exhaustion unit tests. Power-loss vs process-crash documented honestly (fsync-durable, disk-dependent).\\n- P1 WINDOWS DACL: `verifyOwner` now audits owner SID plus every DACL allow entry (null/empty/deny-only/unknown-type fail closed); creation paths install protected owner-only DACLs (`secureStaged`); Unix mode checks abstracted via `platformModeOK` (exact 0700/0600 preserved). Pure `ownerOnlyGrants` evaluator tested on darwin (9 cases). No Windows runner exists here: evidence is GOOS=windows build + vet clean, unit tests, and an explicit stated bound (no invented runtime pass).\\n- P2 EXCLUSION: `ExcludedFromReplication` gains the joint marker; new `MatchExcludedFromReplication` (staging prefixes, fail-closed escapes) and `ExcludedConfigDirName` (.bak./.pre-rollback./.ax-config-*) with custody-walk + published-backup-name tests. No in-repo replication/snapshot/export-of-state surface exists (sessadapter/localstore/dirnode do not touch host-channel); outcome hands consumers + required tests to future export surfaces. Config claim corrected: 4 semantic narrowing + 1 label-precision kill (label plant marked LABEL-PRECISION in-table).\\n- ROW 13: new production `LoadCoherent` (config+trust under one shared hold) + serialization test.\\n- VALIDATION (rerun this run, exit 0): gofmt clean; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./... -count=1` all ok (281 top-level PASS across hosttrust/config/peeridentity/secprim); `-cover` hosttrust 77.8 config 93.1 peeridentity 97.5 secprim 94.4; `-race` on hosttrust+config ok; tracecheck ok; catalog v0.6.0 -check ok; linux+windows amd64 builds ok; `git diff --check` clean; refusal-inventory audit green (new sites covered by direct revalidation/helper tests); census green. Mutation batteries rerun exact-source: hosttrust 18 narrowing KILLED + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label KILLED + neutral passed (manifests bound to a89328c in mutations-*-rework/).\\n- STATUS: ready for review, worktree UNCOMMITTED for handoff snapshot. `task-board validate` shows 231 pre-existing board-wide ledger-mirror issues, none referencing this task.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9529,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2383,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
