{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dd8f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa74-c329-7d72-8811-c1901bb53d47"},"sequence":3362,"recorded_at":1780531400006719,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aaac-7b8a-7022-bb2e-ecd0ff65779a"},"task_id":"01a0aaac-7b8a-7022-bb2e-ecd0ff65779a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aaac-7b8a-7022-bb2e-ecd0ff65779a","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-76-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"^## 2026\\\" LOGBOOK.md | tail -n 5; echo \\\"===\\\"; git diff HEAD --stat -- LOGBOOK.md; git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook sections and diff\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"504:## 2026-09-03\\n797:## 2026-09-02\\n1039:## 2026-09-02 — BUG-260902-2faftr: a name blacklist is not secret detection\\n1106:## 2026-09-01\\n1272:## 2026-09-10 (later)\\n===\\n LOGBOOK.md | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+)\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 57207fc..91bd9f0 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,47 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-16\\n+\\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\\n+- F1: pending joint-commit marker is now a general admission barrier (`convergeLocked` + shared-to-exclusive dance `lockForConvergedRead`): every read/admission/transaction entry point converges or refuses before exposing a snapshot. Surviving stores converge exactly like reopened ones; stale bindings compare against the recovered generation (never refreshed). Real child-process crash tests (exit 77) cover surviving + reopened × apply + rollback, marker cleanup, and intervened refusal with marker kept.\\n+- F2: lock init is atomic non-replacing (O_CREAT|O_EXCL / CREATE_NEW via `FileSystem.CreateExclusive`); losers open the existing inode. Existing-file verify retries 500ms for the create-to-secure window; non-regular refuses immediately. Deterministic cross-process first-open test pins returnedWhileHeld=false + sameInode=true; the replacing-rename mutant restores the exact reviewer failure shape.\\n+- F3: native Windows custody tests written (7, build-tagged; vet + test-compile pass, runtime unverified); config backups classified (byte-exact config copies, 0600, excluded names; Windows backup DACLs a stated bound); row-21 handoff persisted with per-surface API/test obligations + notes on all 7 owned tasks, diagnostics explicitly unowned.\\n+- MUTANT LESSON: a JointCommit converge-ignore mutant survives because the staged-marker refusal backstops it — error-ignoring mutants are unobservable where a file-level backstop stands. Paired instead: joint-converge-skip (call-site, killed) + recover-forward-no-bump (narrowing, kills 8 named convergence tests).\\n+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 25 narrowing + 1 call-site killed + neutral passed; config 4 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; full local CI replicated green (test/race/cover/tracecheck/catalog/cigate/fuzz-13/fixtures/claims/windows-compile). 19 of 21 AC rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) bounded, not passed.\\n+\\n+## 2026-09-10 (refresh)\\n+\\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 refresh — story base moved c1eff01 to a89328c (trunk 8cf4aaa + v0.6.0 adoption)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2653,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 664,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
