{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ddbb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa74-c329-7d72-8811-c1901bb53d47"},"sequence":3384,"recorded_at":1780531400006763,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aaac-a8d0-7e10-9613-7f213141236a"},"task_id":"01a0aaac-a8d0-7e10-9613-7f213141236a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aaac-a8d0-7e10-9613-7f213141236a","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-16\n-\n-### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\n+## 2026-09-16\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\n+- F1: `JointCommit` takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the SAME exclusive hold (`compensateLocked`): marker re-read pin-for-pin, config hash must equal the replacement pin, restore result verified against the source pin before the abort. No reader/writer/boundary can converge between failure and restore. The unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` is deleted. Original CR5 probe RED (exit 1, quoted failure) pre-fix; post-fix its in-seam convergence blocks in `flock` (timeout dump proves the hold) and the ported `TestApplyV4CompensationCannotOverwriteConvergedCommit` pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\n+- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\n+- INTERLEAVINGS: 6 deterministic gated-restore race tests (apply/rollback × reader/writer/held-boundary) + 2 production-entry clean-abort tests + 8 hosttrust compensation tests (tamper/corrupt/unreadable marker, noop+wrong-bytes restore verification, fail-after-write, source-present skip). TEST BUG FOUND BY RACE SUITE ITSELF: boundary tests deadlocked reading trust post-seam on the main goroutine — request now binds pre-seam with a comment.\n+- EVIDENCE: hosttrust battery 30 narrowing (incl. 4 compensate-*) + neutral passed; config 6 semantic + 1 label + neutral passed; all plants pre-verified count==1 with exits from subprocess return codes. Full local CI replicated green (26 ok, 0 FAIL, 1 pre-existing SKIP; race 26 ok; cover hosttrust 77.9/config 93.3; tracecheck/catalog-6/cigate-contracts-6/claims-6/targets-2/fuzz-13/fixtures 51+59 zero-skip/windows-compile). 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; rows 15/21 retained bounded per CR5.\n+- BOUNDS RESTATED: verifyLockFile 500ms retry rechecks custody without pinning an inode (no external-replacement claim); power-loss beyond fsync unproven; Windows runtime unverified; diagnostics export unowned; spurious-bump corner aborts fail-safe.\n+\n+### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev5 — CR4 surviving-reader + lock-init findings repaired\n","final_result":true}}}
