{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e181","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa74-c329-7d72-8811-c1901bb53d47"},"sequence":3867,"recorded_at":1780531400007729,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e52fa573-a598-4d15-9493-65cb4f83069f"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nTASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 is complete. The CR5 finding (unlocked `restoreSourceAfterJointFailure` overwriting a converged Config4 at an unchanged generation) is repaired as a class: `JointCommit` now takes the restore closure and compensates a failed bump under the same exclusive hold, revalidating marker pins and config hashes before restoring and aborting. The original probe reproduced RED pre-fix (exit 1, quoted failure); post-fix its interleave blocks in `flock` and the ported test pins the race as goroutine-vs-gated-restore.\n\nWhat shipped, all verified this run:\n- 12-row write-path census (attached outcome) + committed static gate with firing controls; legacy-migrate fail-closed row pinned by a new test.\n- 8 hosttrust compensation tests, 6 deterministic apply/rollback race tests (reader/writer/held-boundary), 2 production-entry clean-abort tests — full suite 26 ok, race 26 ok, no data races.\n- Mutation batteries on exact final source: hosttrust 29 narrowing + 1 call-site killed, config 6 semantic + 1 label killed, both neutral controls passed, all 39 plants matched exactly once with subprocess exits; preserve-token order-swap mutant killed behaviorally only.\n- Full local CI replicated green (tracecheck, catalog freshness, cigate 6/6+6/6+2/2, fuzz 13/13, fixtures 51+59 zero-skip, Windows compile/vet); 7 original reviewer probes re-pass; preservation re-verified (RPC 15/15 + 11/11, checkpointed SSH/peer untouched).\n- AC: 19 of 21 rows driven; rows 15 (Windows runtime) and 21 (consumers) retained bounded exactly as CR5 accounted them.\n\nCandidate left uncommitted at checkpoint `a89328c`; outcomes `results-rev6.md`, `write-path-census-rev6.md`, `producer-evidence-rev6.tar.gz` attached; checklist 22/22; status `to-review`.","reason":null}}
